/E (Espressif's ESP32 family has grown from a single Wi-Fi/Bluetooth microcontroller into a broad portfolio of System-on-Chips \(SoCs\) spanning two CPU architectures, multiple connectivity profiles, and price points from under $1 to several dollars in volume. This section surveys the core variants relevant to general embedded and IoT project work, compares them side-by-side, and weighs the ESP32 family against traditional microcontrollers such as the STM32 and ATmega328P.)
/Pg 11 0 R
